# Nautilus DevOps — Redis Kubernetes Deployment Recovery

## Project Overview

The Nautilus DevOps team experienced an outage affecting an existing Redis application deployed on a Kubernetes cluster.

The Redis Deployment, named `redis-deployment`, had stopped functioning after incorrect configuration changes were introduced.

The objective was to investigate the failing pods, identify the configuration errors, repair the Deployment, and verify that the Redis application returned to a healthy running state.

## Environment

| Component | Configuration |
|---|---|
| Platform | Kubernetes |
| Access host | jump-host |
| Namespace | default |
| Deployment | redis-deployment |
| Container | redis-container |
| Correct Docker image | redis:alpine |
| ConfigMap | redis-config |
| Container port | 6379 |
| Desired replicas | 1 |

## 1. Initial Investigation

Inspected the Deployment and existing pods:

```bash
kubectl get deployment redis-deployment -o wide
kubectl get pods -o wide
kubectl describe deployment redis-deployment
```

### Initial Deployment Status

```text
NAME               READY   UP-TO-DATE   AVAILABLE
redis-deployment   0/1     1            0
```

The pod was not running:

```text
NAME                                READY   STATUS
redis-deployment-795ffcb56c-bf5n4   0/1     ContainerCreating
```

## 2. Identifying the Configuration Errors

Kubernetes events revealed the first problem:

```text
Warning  FailedMount

MountVolume.SetUp failed for volume "config":
configmap "redis-cofig" not found
```

Listing the available ConfigMaps:

```bash
kubectl get configmaps
```

Output:

```text
NAME           DATA   AGE
kube-root-ca.crt  1   77m
redis-config     2    2m39s
```

The Deployment referenced `redis-cofig`, but the existing ConfigMap was named `redis-config`.

The Deployment YAML also revealed an incorrect Docker image:

```yaml
image: redis:alpin
```

### Root Causes

Two mistakes were identified:

1. Incorrect ConfigMap reference: `redis-cofig` instead of `redis-config`.
2. Incorrect Docker image tag: `redis:alpin` instead of `redis:alpine`.

## 3. Applying the Fixes

### Correcting the Redis image

```bash
kubectl set image deployment/redis-deployment \
  redis-container=redis:alpine
```

Result:

```text
deployment.apps/redis-deployment image updated
```

### Correcting the ConfigMap reference

```bash
kubectl patch deployment redis-deployment \
  --type=strategic \
  -p '{"spec":{"template":{"spec":{"volumes":[{"name":"config","configMap":{"name":"redis-config"}}]}}}}'
```

Result:

```text
deployment.apps/redis-deployment patched
```

Both changes were applied directly to the existing Deployment.

